  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-3378f03f11bcf3b9": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-579",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The Assyrians were famous for their rich and costly apparel. The expression “Assyrian garments” became synonymous with elegant and expensive clothing. Bonomi says: “The robes of the Assyrians were generally ample and flowing, but differed in form from those of the Egyptians and t…"
      },
      "c-748f47442bf6c4f8": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-580",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Here is a manifest reference to those wonderful mural sculptures which, after being buried for centuries amid the ruins of the palaces and temples whose walls they once adorned, have been brought to light by the perseverance and skill of modern explorers. It is not at all improba…"
      },
      "c-f4e5d5a84eef4b58": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-581",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "These mutilations were common among the Chaldeans and Persians. Among the former adulterers were punished in this manner, which fact is doubtless the basis of the reference in the text."
      }
    },
